From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] comctl32: keep the taskbar background behind the Start image

Purpose: draw the rounded right corners of the Luna Start button over the
taskbar, not over a classic face colour. Wine's themed push button refills
its rectangle with the WM_CTLCOLORBTN brush after DrawThemeParentBackground,
following tests on later Windows versions. The XP taskbar answers with the
COLOR_BTNFACE brush, which left light corners around the transparent part
of the Start image. Skip the refill only for the isolated
Win4WineStartButton class created by the opted-in external taskbar; other
buttons keep the existing behaviour. Verified by comparing the taskbar
pixels with the reference XP machine. No Microsoft binary is changed.

diff --git a/dlls/comctl32/button.c b/dlls/comctl32/button.c
index be0a00e..6958099 100644
--- a/dlls/comctl32/button.c
+++ b/dlls/comctl32/button.c
@@ -2848,9 +2848,13 @@ static void PB_ThemedPaint(HTHEME theme, const BUTTON_INFO *infoPtr, HDC hDC, in
     {
         DrawThemeParentBackground(infoPtr->hwnd, hDC, NULL);
         /* Tests show that the brush from WM_CTLCOLORBTN is used for filling background after a
-         * DrawThemeParentBackground() call */
-        brush = (HBRUSH)SendMessageW(parent, WM_CTLCOLORBTN, (WPARAM)hDC, (LPARAM)infoPtr->hwnd);
-        FillRect(hDC, &bgRect, brush ? brush : GetSysColorBrush(COLOR_BTNFACE));
+         * DrawThemeParentBackground() call. The XP taskbar answers with the classic face
+         * brush, while XP keeps its themed background in the Start image's rounded corners. */
+        if (!external_start_button(infoPtr))
+        {
+            brush = (HBRUSH)SendMessageW(parent, WM_CTLCOLORBTN, (WPARAM)hDC, (LPARAM)infoPtr->hwnd);
+            FillRect(hDC, &bgRect, brush ? brush : GetSysColorBrush(COLOR_BTNFACE));
+        }
     }
     DrawThemeBackground(theme, hDC, BP_PUSHBUTTON, state, &bgRect, NULL);
 
